From 9b1b3b65ddcd9987fb4560b3daa2b977aec02e6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 18:55:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Localize the manuscript notebook's configuration, add a
 kernel preset

Every knob the manuscript simulation has now lives in one Configuration
block at the top of smi_manuscript_60deg.m: the kernel, kappa, the crossing
angles and first axis, NREP, SNR_LIST, LMAX_LIST, LMAX_GT, CS_PHASE, the
protocol filename, the quadrature size, the seed, and the regularizer
settings. Nothing below that block needs editing to retune the experiment
and nothing in it has to be looked up elsewhere.

Three stateless utilities are still shared with mc_config.m -- pick_grid,
rotate_about and load_protocol_file -- because they are machinery rather
than settings, and copying them is how the notebook and gen_montecarlo.m
would drift on the fibre-axis convention and the protocol reader. mc_config
gains load_protocol_file so the protocol filename can be a knob in the
notebook while there is still only one reader and one normalisation warning.

The settings are local in both directions: changing them here does not
change gen_montecarlo.m or sweep_nonneg.m, which keep their own values, so
a manuscript figure and the published pipeline can be retuned independently.

KERNEL_PRESET selects the tissue and flows into figure titles, printed
tables and exported filenames, so two runs cannot be confused:

  healthy_wm  [0.60 2.0 2.0 0.50 0.02]   extra-axonal 0.38
  edema       [0.10 2.4 2.7 1.15 0.35]   extra-axonal 0.55

The edema kernel is shaped from a fitted kernel, which is why the
diffusivities are not round and why Depar exceeds Da. Two values depart from
the fit as supplied and the file says why in place:

